airs of electron dots, and the nitrogen atoms have one lone pair of electron dots.\"><br>(e)<br><img src=\"/media/ch07/CNX_Chem_07_03_Impbioanse_img.jpg\" alt=\"A Lewis structure is shown. A carbon atom is single bonded to three oxygen atoms. Two of those oxygen atoms are each single bonded to a hydrogen atom. Each oxygen atom has two lone pairs of electron dots.\">"
